# Keep junk and bulky artifacts out of the build context / image. The production Dockerfile
# copies only src/ (+ requirements.txt) and Dockerfile.test additionally copies tests/ +
# scripts/ + pytest.ini, so most of this is belt-and-braces.
#
# THREE things are deliberately NOT ignored, and each would break something if it were:
#   * tests/ and scripts/  — the tester image needs them in its build context.
#   * web/                 — C13's node:20-alpine stage builds the SPA from it. Only its
#                            install/build output (node_modules, dist) is excluded, and
#                            excluding those is what keeps a host-side `npm install` from
#                            shipping a few hundred MB of context to the daemon on every build.
#   * schema.graphql       — a COMMITTED build output. C3 exports the SDL to it and a test
#                            fails when the committed file drifts from the live schema, so the
#                            tester image has to be able to COPY it.

# VCS
.git
.gitignore

# Planning docs and the spec. `project_requirments.md` is spelled that way upstream (missing an
# `e`); listed literally so the glob is not the only thing standing between it and the image.
*.md
README.md
plan.md
project_requirments.md

# Python caches / build artifacts
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov
build
dist
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv
venv
env
ENV

# Secrets / env — a real .env must never be baked into an image layer. Compose reads it at run
# time via `env_file`, which is the correct seam. `.env.example` is excluded too: it is a
# committed template for humans, and nothing in either image ever reads it.
.env
.env.*

# Node install/build output (see the note above about why web/ ITSELF stays in context)
node_modules
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/build
.vite
.parcel-cache

# Local data (sqlite scratch files, exports, scratch results)
data/
*.db
*.sqlite3

# OS / logs
.DS_Store
*.log
